    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive strategy today hinges on two pillars of production: **Kyle Tucker** (71.92) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.76). **Kyle Tucker** enters as our top play, benefiting from a favorable 4.52 xERA matchup against Phillips. His ability to anchor the 5-hole while maintaining high-efficiency output makes him an indispensable start. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** thrives against Bradish; despite a slight platoon penalty, the strength of the matchup allows him to remain an elite-tier threat. While **Gunnar Henderson** (59.64) and **Heliot Ramos** (59.44) hover just below the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, they remain pivotal to our effort to secure volume in Roto categories, especially with **Gunnar Henderson** providing essential utility across the diamond.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult decision centered on **Coby Mayo**, who finished at 38.79. Despite a solid base projection, he was benched for failing to clear the 40.0 \"Zebras Floor,\" largely due to the stiff challenge presented by Miles\u2019 3.20 xERA. Meanwhile, our lineup construction relies heavily on speed and efficiency. **Henry Bolte** (50.15) and **Sam Antonacci** (51.29) have been slotted into high-leverage leadoff spots to capitalize on their sprint profiles, though both face pressure from the respectable 3.53 xERA of Bryan Woo. We are monitoring **Jackson Merrill** (46.40) closely; while his platoon disadvantage against Perdomo is significant, the favorable wind conditions provided a necessary 10% boost to his efficiency score, keeping him in the lineup over bench options like **Dominic Smith**.\n\nRisks remain present across the board, particularly with several lineups still pending. We are proceeding with the assumption that **Drake Baldwin** (48.90), **Tommy White** (43.03), and **Luis Lara** (50.64) occupy their projected spots; any shift in the batting order could necessitate a recalibration of their expected output. Furthermore, while the current roster is healthy, the ongoing absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages** on the IL continue to cap our ceiling in SB and power categories. We will monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Wade Meckler** to ensure no late-breaking platoon adjustments are required to protect our daily game caps.",
